#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: 6 grapes 40
#> pause: 45
#> must: 1 apples 12
#> must: 4 dates 16
#> must: 6 grapes 40
#> not: 2 bananas 30
#> not: 3 cherries 7
#> source: 1~3p
# 17. GNU address forms. Sheet: "first~step" matches every step-th line from first;
# "addr1,+N" matches addr1 and the N lines after it; "addr1,~N" matches addr1 up to
# the next line whose number is a multiple of N. 1~3 selects 1, 4, 7; /figs/,+1
# selects 5 and 6 (kiwis and figs are each printed once: both commands may select them).
# Try: change /figs/,+1 to /figs/,~4: the range ends at line 8, the next multiple of 4.
#ARGS -n
1~3p
/figs/,+1p

#DATA
1 apples 12
2 bananas 30
3 cherries 7
4 dates 16
5 figs 25
6 grapes 40
7 kiwis 18
8 lemons 22
